          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong generalized graph
            in the sense of
            %a{:href => "#HRY"} HRY
            is a generalization of the notion of a pseudograph given at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph"} graph
            (see in particular
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/graph#definition_in_terms_of_action_on_a_set_of_halfedges"} Definition in terms action on a set of half edges
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wheeled+graph"} wheeled graph
            which is a generalization of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+pseudograph"} directed pseudograph
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+pseudograph"} directed pseudograph
            is the notion of an “exceptional cell,” which should be thought of as a set of half edges which have no vertices.
          %p A generalized graph can be visualized as a set of vertices with half edges attached to them, a rule for attaching half edges to glue the vertices together, and potentially some half edges (flags) that are attached to only one or zero vertices. For instance, a particularly simple generalized graph is one with no vertices and one edge.
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            The following is Definition 2.2 of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#HRY"} HRY
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              A generalized graph
              %math#mathml_f8f2abeaf4b3d1fba96146a1e11cdbd2556eb4f6_1.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              is a finite set
              %math#mathml_f8f2abeaf4b3d1fba96146a1e11cdbd2556eb4f6_2.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Flag
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Flag(G)
              with:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a partition of
                  %math#mathml_f8f2abeaf4b3d1fba96146a1e11cdbd2556eb4f6_3.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Flag
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                          %mrow
                            %mi α
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi A
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mi α
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Flag(G)=\coprod_{\alpha\in A} F_\alpha
                  into
                  %strong cells
                  with
                  %math#mathml_f8f2abeaf4b3d1fba96146a1e11cdbd2556eb4f6_4.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  finite,
              %li
                %p
                  a distinguished partition subset
                  %math#mathml_f8f2abeaf4b3d1fba96146a1e11cdbd2556eb4f6_5.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mi ϵ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_\epsilon
                  called the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %strong exceptional cell
              %li
                %p
                  an involution
                  %math#mathml_f8f2abeaf4b3d1fba96146a1e11cdbd2556eb4f6_6.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ι
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota
                  satisfying
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math#mathml_f8f2abeaf4b3d1fba96146a1e11cdbd2556eb4f6_7.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ι
                          %msub
                            %mi F
                            %mi ϵ
                          %mo ⊆
                          %msub
                            %mi F
                            %mi ϵ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota F_\epsilon\subseteq F_\epsilon
              %li
                %p
                  and a free involution
                  %math#mathml_f8f2abeaf4b3d1fba96146a1e11cdbd2556eb4f6_8.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi π
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
                  on the set of
                  = succeed "-fixed" do
                    %math#mathml_f8f2abeaf4b3d1fba96146a1e11cdbd2556eb4f6_9.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ι
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math#mathml_f8f2abeaf4b3d1fba96146a1e11cdbd2556eb4f6_10.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi F
                            %mi ϵ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_\epsilon
          %p
            Given a generalized graph
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_f8f2abeaf4b3d1fba96146a1e11cdbd2556eb4f6_11.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a{:href => "#HRY"} HRY
            gives some useful terminology:
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %ol
              %li
                The elements of
                %math#mathml_f8f2abeaf4b3d1fba96146a1e11cdbd2556eb4f6_12.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Flag
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Flag(G)
                are called
                = succeed "." do
                  %strong flags
                %strong ordinary flag
                (resp.
                = succeed ")." do
                  %strong exceptional flag
              %li
                Call
                %math#mathml_f8f2abeaf4b3d1fba96146a1e11cdbd2556eb4f6_13.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                an
                %strong ordinary graph
                if
                %math#mathml_f8f2abeaf4b3d1fba96146a1e11cdbd2556eb4f6_14.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mi ϵ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_\epsilon
                is empty.
              %li
                Each non-exceptional partition subset
                %math#mathml_f8f2abeaf4b3d1fba96146a1e11cdbd2556eb4f6_15.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mi α
                      %mo ≠
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mi ϵ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_\alpha\neq F_\epsilon
                is called a
                = succeed "." do
                  %strong vertex
                = succeed "." do
                  %math#mathml_f8f2abeaf4b3d1fba96146a1e11cdbd2556eb4f6_16.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Vt
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vt(G)
                = succeed "." do
                  %strong isolated vertex
                %strong adjacent to
                or
                %strong attached to
                that vertex.
              %li
                An
                = succeed "-fixed" do
                  %math#mathml_f8f2abeaf4b3d1fba96146a1e11cdbd2556eb4f6_17.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ι
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota
                %strong leg
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math#mathml_f8f2abeaf4b3d1fba96146a1e11cdbd2556eb4f6_18.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                = succeed "." do
                  %math#mathml_f8f2abeaf4b3d1fba96146a1e11cdbd2556eb4f6_19.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Leg
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
